<header>
  <p class="meta">WORKING DRAFT · REVISED OCTOBER 20, 2026 · ELIGIBILITY AND INTAKE</p>
  <h1>Membership Operations Blueprint</h1>
  <p class="lede">How people become members, drawn so the election and membership committee can confirm it. Once confirmed, the same page becomes the requirements for choosing or building software. Voting is a separate process and is out of scope here.</p>
</header>

<section aria-label="Core rules">
  <div class="rules">
    <div class="rule"><span class="big">$600+</span><span class="what">Individual member</span><span class="why">Given in the giving year, Dec 1 to Nov 30. Up to $1,199.</span></div>
    <div class="rule"><span class="big">$1,200+</span><span class="what">Household member</span><span class="why">Spouses living at the same street address, combined. Adds spouse, kids 18 to 26 and parents.</span></div>
    <div class="rule"><span class="big">Monthly</span><span class="what">Invitations</span><span class="why">Treasurer's report, committee scrub, then one email with a one-time link.</span></div>
    <div class="rule"><span class="big">60 days</span><span class="what">Link lifetime</span><span class="why">Expires on submit, after 60 days or on Dec 10, whichever is first.</span></div>
    <div class="rule"><span class="big">Dec 1</span><span class="what">Membership starts</span><span class="why">Lasts one year. Every year starts from scratch.</span></div>
    <div class="rule"><span class="big">~800</span><span class="what">People</span><span class="why">About 200 households, an assumed average of 4 voting people each, a unique email for every person.</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="systems">
  <div class="sec-head">
    <span class="fig-tag">Figure 1 · Systems and data</span>
    <h2>Who and what exchange data</h2>
    <p>The central repository is a Google Sheet for now, and vendor software is investigated later. QuickBooks stays the record of donations. Mailchimp is the email service and sends only what the repository gives it.</p>
