<section id="notices">
  <div class="sec-head">
    <h2>Notices</h2>
    <p>Every message goes by email to a person with a unique address. None of them shows a donation amount. Only the tier, Individual or Household, ever appears.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="tbl">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>When</th><th>To</th><th>What it says</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Monthly send, person on the list as Individual</td><td>Individual</td><td>Invitation with an individual registration link. Valid 60 days, one use.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Monthly send, person or household on the list as Household</td><td>Household primary</td><td>Invitation with a household registration link, to enroll spouse and dependents. Sent to the primary only. Spouse and dependents are not sent an invitation.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>14 days after the invitation, not yet registered</td><td>Invitee</td><td>One reminder. The link is the same.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>A link expired unused, and the person is still on the report</td><td>Invitee</td><td>A new invitation with a fresh link in the next monthly send.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>A registered individual later moves to the Household tier</td><td>Household primary</td><td>Household invitation. The existing record is upgraded.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Registration submitted</td><td>Each member on it</td><td>Confirmation of that person's own record, with the committee's contact details. For a spouse or dependent this is the first email they receive. Children outside 18 to 26 are saved but not emailed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Same</td><td>Household primary</td><td>The full household summary, in addition to their own confirmation.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>A used or expired link is opened</td><td>Person, on screen</td><td>A generic message with the committee's contact details. Not an email.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>A conflict is found, or 60 days pass with no registration</td><td>Committee</td><td>Conflict report and an invited-not-registered count.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="note">Invitations go out through Mailchimp. Confirmations are sent through its Transactional add-on. Out of scope for now: mid-year reminders, renewal emails, lapsed notices and notices to dependents who lose membership.</p>
</section>

<section class="cols" aria-label="Anomalies and open decisions">
  <div>
    <div class="sec-head"><h2>Anomaly report</h2><p>The system flags and the committee decides. Nothing is deleted or blocked automatically.</p></div>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>A person in more than one household</li>
      <li>An email used by more than one person</li>
      <li>A dependent who is already a member or on the donor list</li>
      <li>A child outside 18 to 26 on Dec 1, saved as not a member</li>
      <li>A group number still unresolved on the list loaded to the repository</li>
      <li>Different addresses inside one household</li>
      <li>An invitation with no registration after 60 days</li>
      <li>A donor on the report who matches more than one record</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <div class="sec-head"><h2>Open decisions</h2><p>Answers change the diagrams above.</p></div>
    <ol class="dec">
      <li><span class="id">D1</span><span><b>Tier after a lower year<span class="tag">later phase</span></b><span class="q">A household that gives $600 to $1,199 next year: individual member? Do spouse and dependents lose membership?</span></span></li>
      <li><span class="id">D4</span><span><b>In-kind matches</b><span class="q">Employer matches, goods valued in dollars, or both, and who records the value.</span></span></li>
      <li><span class="id">D5</span><span><b>Household primary after a combine</b><span class="q">The committee names the primary in the scrub. Who is it when a couple crosses $1,200 together?</span></span></li>
      <li><span class="id">D7</span><span><b>Monthly calendar and backup</b><span class="q">Report date, scrub deadline and send date, and who covers when the treasurer or reviewer is away.</span></span></li>
      <li><span class="id">D8</span><span><b>The Nov 30 cutoff</b><span class="q">Gift date or the date entered in QuickBooks.</span></span></li>
      <li><span class="id">D9</span><span><b>Changes mid-year</b><span class="q">Moves, divorces, a dependent who ages out, and a person without email. All go through the committee.</span></span></li>
      <li><span class="id">D15</span><span><b>Building on a Sheet</b><span class="q">A Sheet cannot host forms or issue one-time links by itself. Who builds and maintains the small script that does (a Google Apps Script web app is the likely route), and who owns the Sheet?</span></span></li>
    </ol>
    <p class="note">Closed: D2 (replaced by the scrub), D6 (the link works as soon as it arrives), D10 (an expired invitee is re-invited in the next send), D11 (confirmations use the Mailchimp Transactional add-on), D3 (addresses match as entered), D12 (the repository is a Google Sheet for now), D13 (last pull Nov 30, links expire Dec 10) and D14 (voting is a separate process, out of scope here).</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="assumptions">
  <div class="sec-head">
    <h2>Assumptions register</h2>
    <p>Confirmed items came from the committee. Inference items are mine and need a yes or no. Greyed rows are replaced or deferred.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="tbl">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Assumption</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="mono">A1</td><td>The giving year runs Dec 1 to Nov 30. Membership starts the following Dec 1 and lasts one year. A person is Qualified when the threshold is met and Active from Dec 1.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">A2</td><td>Spouses are assessed together. $1,200 combined makes a household. Otherwise a spouse who gave $600 alone is an individual member, and the other spouse is not a member. Where several people at one address may combine, the committee decides in the scrub.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">A3</td><td>Every registered member must have an email, and each email is unique to one person. A child saved as not a member does not need one. No login or password is created. The email is the identity.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span> <span class="st inf">uniqueness inferred</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">A4</td><td>A parent's status is an honor-system declaration.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">A5</td><td>Child age is a dropdown: under 18, 18 to 26 (eligible), 27 or older. Age is measured on Dec 1 of the membership start year. A child outside 18 to 26 is accepted on the form and saved, but is not a member and is not emailed.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">A6</td><td>A person can belong to only one household.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">A7</td><td>Within a giving year, tiers only move up, from individual to household. An upgrade gets a household link, and the existing record is upgraded.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">A8</td><td>At $600 to $1,199 a person is invited with an individual link. At $1,200 or more the primary is invited with a household link to enroll dependents. Only the primary is invited. Spouses and dependents are never sent a link.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">A9</td><td>Only actual donations and in-kind matches count. Pledges count once paid. No refunds are expected, so no reversal logic.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr class="old"><td class="mono">A10</td><td>Existing members under next year's threshold get a mid-year reminder. When they cross it they get an email to validate eligibility.</td><td><span class="st old">Out of scope</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">A11</td><td>The system reports anomalies to the committee. It flags and does not block.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span> <span class="st inf">flag-only inferred</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">A12</td><td>Donations are the only money in. There are no separate dues.</td><td><span class="st inf">Inference</span></td></tr>
        <tr class="old"><td class="mono">A13</td><td>Manual review of non-matches is done by the treasurer or the committee.</td><td><span class="st old">Superseded by B2, B3</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">A14</td><td>The invitation link proves the primary owns their email. Other household members' emails are checked by the confirmation email each of them receives, not before.</td><td><span class="st inf">Inference</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">A15</td><td>No donation amount appears in any message, form, the monthly report or the repository. Only the tier, Individual or Household, is shown.</td><td><span class="st inf">Inference</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">A16</td><td>About 200 households with an assumed average of 4 voting people each, about 800 people. Individual members are inside that count.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr class="old"><td class="mono">A17</td><td>A returning household requalifies by giving again and gets a renewal email to verify what is on file.</td><td><span class="st old">Out of scope</span></td></tr>
        <tr class="old"><td class="mono">A18</td><td>A lapsed primary gets a lapsed email. Their dependents get an email that they have lost membership.</td><td><span class="st old">Out of scope</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">A19</td><td>QuickBooks holds the donation record. The treasurer builds the monthly report from it.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr class="old"><td class="mono">A20</td><td>Intake is hybrid: anyone may register, and a non-match goes to a human.</td><td><span class="st old">Superseded by B1</span></td></tr>
        <tr class="old"><td class="mono">A21</td><td>A non-member who qualifies gets a new member email.</td><td><span class="st old">Superseded by A8</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B1</td><td>No self-registration. Only people on the scrubbed list receive a link.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B2</td><td>Each month the treasurer produces a report by street address with Unique ID, first name, last name, address, email and Household or Individual. The report shows the tier only, never a donation amount. Where several people at one address together pass a threshold, each gets a record with a group number.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B3</td><td>The committee scrub is manual and final. After it, one record is one person or one household, and a combined group has one named primary who receives the household link.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span> <span class="st inf">named primary inferred</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B4</td><td>The scrubbed list is loaded into the central repository. It skips people already invited or registered, issues each person's unique link and exports a file for Mailchimp, which sends once a month.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B5</td><td>A link works once. It expires on submit, 60 days after it is sent, or on Dec 10, whichever is first. A form that fails validation does not use the link up.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B6</td><td>One automatic reminder goes out 14 days after the invitation. After that, nothing.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B7</td><td>The last pull from QuickBooks is on Nov 30 and is sent right after. Every link expires on Dec 10, so a link sent after Nov 30 has fewer than 60 days, and the 14-day reminder may not apply. Anyone who registers by Dec 10 starts membership on Dec 1.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span> <span class="st inf">Dec 1 start inferred</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B8</td><td>The repository is the source of truth. Mailchimp holds only what it needs to send.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B9</td><td>The invitation goes to the primary only. When the primary submits, every member listed (spouse, children 18 to 26, parents) gets a confirmation of their own record, which is the first message they receive. The primary also gets the household summary. All include the committee's contact details.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B10</td><td>Changes after submission are made only by the committee, and each edit is logged with who and when. A used or expired link shows the committee's contact details.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B11</td><td>Dependent conflicts, such as someone already a member, are flagged to the committee and not rejected on the spot.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B12</td><td>Dependents' data, including minors, is visible only to committee admins. A retention period is set later.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B13</td><td>The repository guarantees a unique email per person. Voting is a separate process, kept out of scope here.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B14</td><td>Renewals, mid-year reminders and lapse notices are out of scope for this phase.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B15</td><td>Each year starts from scratch, so a new invitation is needed every year.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B16</td><td>A person whose link expired unused, and who is still on the treasurer's report, is re-invited with a fresh link in the next monthly send.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B17</td><td>Invitations are sent through Mailchimp. Confirmations are sent through its Transactional add-on.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B18</td><td>Voting is its own process and flow, designed separately and out of scope for this blueprint.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B19</td><td>The treasurer's report matches donors on the address exactly as entered. If addresses differ at all, they are separate records and are not grouped. Spouses at different addresses are separate households.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B20</td><td>The committee can combine, scrub and change records as needed, including linking records the report did not match.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B21</td><td>A CRM-level system may be needed later. It is not in scope now, but the repository's data should be exportable.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B22</td><td>The central repository is a Google Sheet for now. Vendor software is investigated later.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B23</td><td>The Sheet is shared with a small number of committee admins only. The registration form runs outside the Sheet, writes to it through a script, and the script also issues and checks links, keeps the edit log and sends the confirmation.</td><td><span class="st inf">Inference</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">B24</td><td>A household can include children outside 18 to 26 on Dec 1. The form is accepted and their information is saved. They are not members, no email is sent to them, and their email is optional.</td><td><span class="st">Confirmed</span></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

